Upstream bug: WlrBufferConstraints.dma field's cfg gate is missing the
udev feature, but three call sites in src/core/handlers/wlr_screencopy.rs
and src/protocols/wlr_screencopy.rs already guard their access to it with
#[cfg(any(feature = "winit", feature = "udev"))] — meaning a udev-only
build (no winit, no x11) fails with "no field `dma` on type
`WlrBufferConstraints`" since the struct field itself doesn't exist in
that configuration. Widening the field's gate to also include "udev"
matches what the rest of the code already expects.

--- a/src/protocols/wlr_screencopy.rs	2026-07-04 12:19:58.761019085 +0530
+++ b/src/protocols/wlr_screencopy.rs	2026-07-04 12:19:58.762147765 +0530
@@ -150,7 +150,7 @@
     pub size: Size<i32, BufferCoords>,
     /// Available SHM formats, and rowstride for that format
     pub shm: Vec<(wl_shm::Format, u32)>,
-    #[cfg(any(feature = "winit", feature = "x11"))]
+    #[cfg(any(feature = "winit", feature = "x11", feature = "udev"))]
     /// Available linux-dmabuf formats, if any
     pub dma: Vec<Fourcc>,
 }
